<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sido</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sido was a Suebian king of the 1st century CE who, with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vangio">Vangio</a>, overthrew their uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vannius">Vannius</a> in 50 CE and shared his kingdom north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. The brothers remained loyal clients of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, Sido and another Suebian king, Italicus, brought warriors to fight for Vespasian's side in the Roman civil war of 69 CE, including at the second battle of Bedriacum.</p></div>
